/F2 9 Tf (## 1. Executive Summary) Tj /F1 8 Tf T*
(A Software-Defined Vessel \(SDV\) cannot treat human crew availability as a mere scheduling annotation: ) Tj T*
(crew count directly governs **which physical payload transitions are admissible**, **which manual deck) Tj T*
( evolutions can be staffed**, **whether at-sea vehicle replacement \(A' window\) is physically safe**, ) Tj T*
(and **how fault recovery escalates when telemetry degrades or a payload overconsumes**. In `sdv-) Tj T*
(resource-governor`, human crew availability, flight-deck clearance \(`deck_clear`\), and port-only ) Tj T*
(installation constraints are enforced as hard operational guards inside `scheduling.py`, ) Tj T*
(`admission.py`, and `replay.py`.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(---) Tj T*
() Tj T*
